    {"en", "presets\n  Lists the transfer presets from the user configuration.\n  A preset is stored with 'savepreset <name> <setting>...'\n  (transfer=binary|ascii|automatic, preservetime=on|off|all,\n  neweronly, speed=<KB/s>, resumesupport=on|off|<KB>,\n  permissions=<octal>|off|fromfile, host=, user=, remotedir=,\n  localdir=, mask=); 'rmspreset <name>' removes one.\n  'option preset <name>' makes a preset the default for the\n  following transfer commands, 'option preset off' disables\n  presets for this session (even matching rules); a stored\n  site loads its own when it is opened.", "presets\n  Lists the transfer presets from the user configuration.\n  A preset is stored with 'savepreset <name> <setting>...'\n  (transfer=binary|ascii|automatic, preservetime=on|off|all,\n  neweronly, speed=<KB/s>, resumesupport=on|off|<KB>,\n  permissions=<octal>|off|fromfile, host=, user=, remotedir=,\n  localdir=, mask=); 'rmspreset <name>' removes one.\n  'option preset <name>' makes a preset the default for the\n  following transfer commands, 'option preset off' disables\n  presets for this session (even matching rules); a stored\n  site loads its own when it is opened."},
    {"en", "property <file> -get=NAME | property <file> -set=NAME=VALUE\n  Reads or writes one WebDAV dead property of a file, in this\n  client's own namespace. '-get' prints 'NAME is not set' when\n  the server says the property does not exist.", "property <file> -get=NAME | property <file> -set=NAME=VALUE\n  Reads or writes one WebDAV dead property of a file, in this\n  client's own namespace. '-get' prints 'NAME is not set' when\n  the server says the property does not exist."},
    {"en", "put [ <switches> ] <file> [ <file>... ] [ <target> ]\n  Uploads files; the switches of 'get' (on uploads,\n  -permissions without a value keeps the local file's own\n  mode on the server); -append adds to the remote file\n  instead of replacing it (native SFTP only, and not\n  together with -resume); -latest uploads only the newest\n  local file the command named.", "put [ <switches> ] <file> [ <file>... ] [ <target> ]\n  Uploads files; the switches of 'get' (on uploads,\n  -permissions without a value keeps the local file's own\n  mode on the server); -append adds to the remote file\n  instead of replacing it (native SFTP only, and not\n  together with -resume); -latest uploads only the newest\n  local file the command named."},
